Kernel Follower rebuilds the out-of-tree kernel modules registered with it
for the kernel an OPNsense update installs, before the host reboots onto
it: the kernel's own sources fetched from opnsense/src (or taken from an
archive carried on the machine), each module built from nothing, checked,
and installed with a stamp of the kernel it was built for, the previous
build kept beside it. It runs from the upgrade hook, at every orderly
reboot (bounded), and every five minutes, and removes the sources of
kernels no longer run once the new one has settled.

Where os-xgs-npu is installed, its own two modules stay with its own
follower.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0.1

* routine lines logged once a boot, not every five minutes
* kernel sources: room checked first, an hour between failed fetches of the same kernel, no tree left half written
* a Check never waits for a run; the upgrade hook is bounded
* the fall-back to kernel.old stays while os-xgs-npu's module is built for another kernel
* the page: one status a refresh, the last run's result in the page's language with its reason on hover
* a registration is read one way by follow.sh and by the page
* removal also takes what a self-update left

